==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-day in, day out.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adverb===
{{head|en|adverb|head=[[day]] [[in]], day [[out]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Every day; [[daily]]; [[constantly]] or [[continuously]] (especially, of something that has become [[routine]] or [[monotonous]]).
#: {{ux|en|Even if you like peanut butter sandwiches, eating the same sandwiches '''day in, day out''' will get old.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 26|author=John Crosse|title=When the tide turned to a safer railway...|journal=RAIL|issue=949|page=52|text=There were derailments happening '''day in and day out''', due in part to 'shunting mishaps' but more frequently involving wagons in freight trains due to a combination of poor track and speed.}}

